==Personal life==
[[File:Sarah Hazen Stitt and Kevin Stitt (55104632544).jpg|thumb|Stitt and his wife Sarah Hazen, 2026]]
Stitt is a citizen of the [[Cherokee Nation]] through his great-grandfather, Robert Benton Dawson. Dawson was given land in the [[Skiatook, Oklahoma|Skiatook]] area because of his tribal citizenship, and the land is still in the family, now owned by an uncle of Stitt's.<ref name="auto4"/> The veracity of his claim to [[Cherokee ancestry]] had previously been questioned due to the [[Cherokee Nation (1794–1907)|Cherokee Nation]]'s failed attempt to [[tribal disenrollment|remove]] Robert Benton Dawson from the [[Dawes Rolls]] around 1900 for allegedly having bribed a tribal official in order for himself and dozens of his relatives to be included in the tribal roll around 1880;<ref>{{Cite web |last= |first= |last2= |first2= |date=2020-02-24 |title=The Cherokee Nation once fought to disenroll Gov. Kevin Stitt's ancestors |url=https://www.hcn.org/articles/indigenous-affairs-the-cherokee-nation-once-fought-to-disenroll-gov-kevin-stitts-ancestors |access-date=2023-04-26 |website=www.hcn.org |language=en-us}}</ref> the current Cherokee Nation no longer disputes Stitt's citizenship.<ref>{{Cite news|last=MURPHY|first=SEAN|date=February 29, 2020|title=Oklahoma governor's tribal fight raises ancestry questions|work=ABC News|url=https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/wireStory/oklahoma-governors-tribal-fight-raises-ancestry-questions-69306593}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|date=Feb 24, 2020|title=The Cherokee Nation once fought to disenroll Gov. Kevin Stitt's ancestors|work=High Country News|url=https://www.hcn.org/articles/indigenous-affairs-the-cherokee-nation-once-fought-to-disenroll-gov-kevin-stitts-ancestors}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|date=March 2, 2020|title=Oklahoma governor won't let Indian ancestry doubts derail gaming dispute|work=Indianz.com|url=https://www.indianz.com/IndianGaming/2020/03/02/oklahoma-governor-wont-let-indian-ancest.asp}}</ref> Stitt's maternal grandparents were dairy farmers in Skiatook. His paternal grandfather was the head veterinarian at the Oklahoma City Stockyards.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.oklahomafarmreport.com/wire/news/2018/07/00153_KevinStittTalksAgIssues07252018b_051515.php#.W9PTcBNKiL8|title=Oklahoma Farm Report – Gubernatorial Candidate Kevin Stitt Says Ag will Always have a Seat at the Table in His Administration|website=www.oklahomafarmreport.com|access-date=October 27, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181027101318/http://www.oklahomafarmreport.com/wire/news/2018/07/00153_KevinStittTalksAgIssues07252018b_051515.php#.W9PTcBNKiL8|archive-date=October 27, 2018|url-status=live}}</ref>

Stitt married [[Sarah Hazen]] on June 1, 1998, and they have six children.<ref name="EOHC" /><ref>{{cite tweet |last=Stitt |first=Kevin |user=GovStitt |number=1134874094581821440 |date=June 1, 2019 |title=For our 21st anniversary, the First Lady and I went fly fishing this morning in the beautiful Beaver Bend state park. #OklaProud @TravelOK |language=en |access-date=December 31, 2022}}</ref> The Stitts are active with the Woodlake Church, an [[Assemblies of God USA]] church in Tulsa.<ref>{{cite web| url=https://okcfox.com/news/local/race-for-governor-kevin-stitt| title=Kevin Stitt: Republican| date=May 31, 2018| access-date=October 16, 2018| archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181016164933/https://okcfox.com/news/local/race-for-governor-kevin-stitt| archive-date=October 16, 2018| url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Woodlake Church |url=https://ag.org/church?g=a2a2b950-ff8c-461d-9a3a-a8210c1a32a0&d=False |access-date=2023-02-08}}</ref> On October 31, 2022, Stitt's 20-year-old son was found intoxicated in a parking lot in [[Guthrie, Oklahoma]], while in possession of firearms, including a gun belonging to his father. No charges were filed, though the [[Logan County, Oklahoma|Logan County]] Sheriff's Office recommended filing charges.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.oklahoman.com/story/news/politics/government/2022/11/19/son-of-oklahoma-gov-kevin-stitt-found-intoxicated-with-guns-no-charges-john-stitt/69662653007/ |title=Son of Oklahoma Gov. Kevin Stitt found intoxicated with guns |publisher=Oklahoman.com |date=2022-01-26 |access-date=2022-11-22}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.oklahoman.com/story/news/politics/government/2022/11/21/oklahoma-gov-kevin-stitt-son-gun-alcohol-charges-halloween/69667288007/ |title=Sheriff recommended charges against Kevin Stitt son in Oct. incident |publisher=Oklahoman.com |date=2020-02-27 |access-date=2022-11-22}}</ref>

Stitt is a fan of the [[Oklahoma City Thunder]]. When the [[2024–25 Oklahoma City Thunder season|2024–25 team]] won the [[2025 NBA Finals]], he was one of many Oklahoma politicians who celebrated the victory.<ref>{{Cite web|title='Always known this day would come': Oklahoma lawmakers react to Thunder winning NBA championship|url=https://www.koco.com/article/thunder-nba-champions-oklahoma-lawmakers/65150585|date=June 23, 2025|access-date=May 6, 2026|website=KOCO}}</ref>

